{"kind":"report","text":"Navigation/visualization research completed for comprehensive dap UI. Goal: connect purpose, commitments/plans, exact changes/code, evidence, publication and future operations across scales; support finding next action, explaining blockers, locating overlap and tracing consequences. Three parallel primary-source investigations plus root vetting; recommendations, not selected features or tested dap usability.\n\nSankey/alluvial/parallel sets are strong candidates for selectable aggregate overviews. Legitimate examples: a fixed cohort of issues at successive dates (distinct issue count), categorical issue/commitment distribution with exclusive axis categories, and explicit recorded relation/change-path incidence counts across purpose→change→code. Numeric widths must identify their unit, denominator, time/frontier, grouping and deduplication. Ten issues, twenty commitments and thirty files are different entities, not one conserved work quantity. Many-to-many joins can multiply tuples; show unique entity counts separately. Pairwise issue-change and change-file links do not prove that a particular file implements a particular issue. Reopens require time-expanded states or an event trace; standard d3-sankey targets acyclic graphs. Include unlinked/unclaimed work explicitly. Source: github.com/d3/d3-sankey; original Parallel Sets paper eagereyes.org/publications/Kosara-TVCG-2006.\n\nComplementary techniques:\n- Focused directed relationship/provenance view: start from search/selected object; expand prerequisites, selected inputs or consequences one typed relation at a time; explain exact subject/evidence/action. Native causal or dependency edges remain distinct from mentions/touches/closes/Git parent edges. Cycles shown, not forced into DAG. Source: dig.cmu.edu/publications/2009-doigraphs.html.\n- Change×file/extent incidence matrix and clustered dependency/overlap matrix: dense cross-cutting relationships, shared areas and cycles using correct edge semantics; a shared file is not a proved text conflict. Cells open contributing records. Classic node-link/matrix study supports task-dependent complementarity, not a universal size threshold (random undirected20/50/100-node experiment): mohammad.ghoniem.info/research/ivs-usability-2005.pdf.\n- Goal/condition×change/evidence requirements matrix: distinguish missing, stale, qualifying, refused and unknown evidence for exact version/extents. Goal coverage needs an explicit relation/criterion; raw counts are not percent complete.\n- Icicle/treemap and stable code atlas: directory hierarchy with named measures and overlays for selected changes/issues/search/review. Stable locations support recurring navigation; path/filebytes/churn/dependency are different measures. Code proximity or co-change is not dependency or causal impact. Sources d3js.org/d3-hierarchy/partition; scg.unibe.ch/research/softwarecartography.\n- UpSet/incidence/hypergraph views: exact intersections of file/extent sets across changes/goals, avoiding false pairwise cliques. Source vdl.sci.utah.edu/publications/2014_infovis_upset/.\n- Storylines/event sequences/swimlanes/aging WIP: repeated review/check cycles, wait vs execution vs unknown external operation, provenance to production. Time positions do not establish causality; define started/finished/cohort before cycle/age metrics. Sources hcil.umd.edu/eventflow/; kanbanguides.org/the-kanban-guide/2025.5/.\n- Small multiples/sparklines: consistently scaled comparison across repositories/services/environments and time windows; health is a timestamped observation, not past check evidence.\n- Hierarchical edge bundling: cross-package coupling overview with exact endpoints on selection; classification and measured width explicit. Source research.tue.nl/en/publications/hierarchical-edge-bundles-visualization-of-adjacency-relations-in/. Consider later if simple overview+focused trace insufficient.\n\nNavigation recommendations: several coordinated views of the same selected authorized record set; aggregate selection opens its literal contributors and carries them to matrix/tree/history/diff/trace; relationship-column browser can expose goal→issue→change→file with clear Back without requiring graph interpretation. Support semantic zoom from grouped purpose/subsystem to records to version/path/line; preserve selection, scope/frontier, relation kinds, filters and metric when switching. Provide search-first for known targets, overview-first for discovery, saved reproducible perspectives, and named query explanation. Pure visualization selection does not mutate room state or switch execution workspace. Edge inspection opens recorded relationship/provenance, node opens canonical home, action invokes exact contextual offered act with requirements/result.\n\nCommon data/access contract: exact node/reference/version identity; typed relation with source evidence and derived/inferred designation; explicit count/aggregation; per-scope/time coverage; selected object-set identity shared across views; bounded aggregate/query/index support rather than browser downloading entire room. Distinguish zero from unloaded/unsupported/unauthorized. Aggregates must not expose restricted nodes/counts. Preserve negative/unlinked records when proving complete authorized coverage. Keep layouts stable, grouping explicit, details progressive; keyboard/table/list equivalent and mobile focused drillthrough. Current verified Git reader/lanes are foundations, not an existing all-relation visualization API.\n\nRecommended prototype comparisons, no implementation commissioned: (1) find unserved goal through Sankey and coverage matrix; (2) select code area, follow issues/changes, examine overlap, open exact diff and return; (3) explain blocked or deployed version with focused provenance/evidence view and temporal trace. Evaluate correct answers, valid attribution, next-action discovery and context restoration with actual sparse/dense/partial fixtures, not preference for chart appearance. Apply current dap design system and Tufte layering/labeling; additional category colors require a reviewed semantic palette, not arbitrary decoration.\n\nEvidence is current official documentation/original research, not hands-on dap testing. No code/source changes, visual prototypes, tests, provider operations, feature adoption or builder reprioritization. No dated note update was requested in this turn.\n"}